description=AMD FidelityFX (FSR) upscaling for Project Zomboid B42, one mod with two loading modes: EITHER add -javaagent pointing at this mod's agent\42.22\fsr-upsc-agent.jar to the launch options (load-time agent, no extra mod needed), OR just keep ZombieBuddy (release 2.x or BETA 3.x) installed and enable this mod - ZombieBuddy loads the jar from mod.info and retransforms the game in place (first launch shows the ZombieBuddy approval dialog, choose persist). World pass renders at a reduced resolution (FidelityFX quality presets) and is resolved with FSR 1 EASU+RCAS, or FSR 2 / FSR 3.1 temporal upscaling (GL compute) with injected sub-pixel camera jitter, depth chain, auto-reactive masks and entity motion vectors, plus optional software frame generation on the present path (FsrControl.fsr2FgTest). Falls back to FSR 1 automatically on any compute fault. Running both modes at once is safe: the second entry detects the armed JVM and stands down. One jar serves both game builds in both modes: the runtime whitelist accepts B42.22 (revision e013dbb529) and B42.21 (revision 4a0e9546ec, rollback). Bundled agent jars under agent\<build>\: agent\42.22 (the unified jar) and agent\42.21 (the proven legacy 42.21 build for rollback players); scripts\install-agent.ps1 picks the matching folder automatically, and the unified jar is mirrored byte-identical at media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar - the copy ZombieBuddy loads through javaJarFile. Any other revision runs stock instead of transforming (runtime hash gate).

Agent jars ship inside this mod folder, one per game build: agent\42.21\ and
agent\42.22\ (javaagent mode), plus the byte-identical media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar
that the ZombieBuddy mode loads through mod.info (javaJarFile/javaPkgName) on
game start. Hook groups, downscale and upscaler settings behave identically in
both modes (ModOptions.ini / fsrupsc.FsrControl from Lua).
